# Slices 3/4 boundary (Opus, 2026-09-27, steps/gate-measure-20260927.md): a composite value
# (`n - 1`) of one named primitive type given to a formal of another now gets the same edge a
# single value has -- l2_check_value_convert_field/l2_emit_value_convert_field type it themselves
# (l2_native_composite_ty, l2_rw_tokens+l2_rw_tyof) and the receiver is called on a copy of the
# whole n-field chain (l2_emit_value_convert_n), the same shape l2_rw_convert already uses at the
# walked root.  n - 1 = 5U fits size_t: `take` runs and the entry is 7.  The refusal is
# unit_s3_arg_conv_compound_range.  Mutant: the edge not emitted -- C converts the composite
# itself, `take` still runs the same way here (every value fits); see the range fixture's mutant.
fn: take (size_t: n) int
    if: n = 5
        return: 7
    return: 0
end: take
fn: go () int
    int: n 6
    return: take(n - 1)
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
